#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""AbGal. Android Batch Guests, Accelerated and Local.

One program for the whole life of a guest: create it from a template, start
it, look at it, stop it again. The SDK, the guests and the logs live under the
folder this file sits in. The SDK tools keep their user files there too, in
android-home/; only adb still keeps its key in ~/.android, see
docs/troubleshooting.md.

  abgal setup                         fetch the SDK into sdk/
  abgal doctor                        check the machine and the SDK
  abgal list                          templates and guests
  abgal create <template>             one guest, named after the template
  abgal create <template> --count 10  ten guests, numbered
  abgal start -n <guest>              start one guest
  abgal start -n <a> -n <b>           start them one after another
  abgal status                        what is on disk and what is running
  abgal stop -n <guest>               stop that guest
  abgal shutdown                      stop every guest and its watch, disks stay
  abgal watch -n <guest>              the temperature watch start runs by itself
  abgal webui                         the browser view, open to the network
  abgal github-runner status          local liveness of the self hosted runners
  abgal github-runner log -n <name>   the runner's own log

Only the Python standard library is used. There is nothing to install and
nothing to package: the file is the program.
"""

